    "method": "Independent reproduction of the nine frozen pre-W8 registry records on the W8 code base: cache files located by SHA-256 and read directly as JSONL; detector re-run at its native operating point over every labelled row (document slices) and every labelled sentence (OpAI-Bench segment slice); FPR/TPR with Wilson 95% CIs, AUROC (pairwise Mann-Whitney, cross-checked against the rank form) and AUPRC (stepwise average precision over distinct score thresholds), all recomputed from scratch with implementations written here. FPR/TPR agreement is by exact k implied by the registry's 4-decimal values; AUROC agreement is to 4 decimals. The recomputed Wilson FPR upper is compared against Worker D's predeclaration \u00a71 values, NOT against the registry's stored CI: the registry's stored FPR CI for the RAID 20261106 record is a bootstrap CI (ci_upper 0.0, degenerate on an all-zero sample) and every stored TPR CI is bootstrap, so those stored CIs cannot be compared to a Wilson CI. The stored CIs are recorded verbatim per record alongside their method.",
